    ("If I ___ you, I would apologise.", "were", ["was", "am", "be"], "Unreal conditions use 'were' for all subjects."),
    ("Neither of the two boys ___ present.", "was", ["were", "are", "have"], "'Neither of' takes a singular verb."),
    ("He has been working here ___ 2015.", "since", ["for", "from", "at"], "'Since' is used with a fixed point in time."),
    ("Each of the students ___ given a certificate.", "was", ["were", "are", "have been"], "'Each' is singular."),
    ("I look forward to ___ you.", "meeting", ["meet", "met", "have met"], "'Look forward to' is followed by a gerund."),
    ("She is senior ___ me.", "to", ["than", "from", "over"], "'Senior' takes 'to', not 'than'."),
    ("We have lived in this city ___ ten years.", "for", ["since", "from", "by"], "'For' is used with a period of time."),
    ("___ honest man is respected everywhere.", "An", ["A", "The", "No article"], "'Honest' begins with a vowel sound, so 'an'."),
    ("He is studying at ___ university in Pune.", "a", ["an", "the", "no article"], "'University' begins with a consonant sound /ju/, so 'a'."),
    ("By the time we arrived, the film ___.", "had started", ["started", "has started", "starts"], "An earlier past action uses the past perfect."),
    ("The teacher, along with her students, ___ going on a trip.", "is", ["are", "were", "have"], "The verb agrees with the main subject 'teacher'."),
    ("I wish I ___ taller.", "were", ["was", "am", "will be"], "A wish about the present uses 'were'."),
    ("Hardly had he left ___ it began to rain.", "when", ["than", "then", "because"], "'Hardly ... when' is the correct pair."),
    ("He is good ___ mathematics.", "at", ["in", "on", "with"], "The idiomatic phrase is 'good at'."),
    ("The bridge was named ___ the architect.", "after", ["from", "to", "on"], "'Named after' means given the name of."),
    ("Please divide the sweets ___ the two children.", "between", ["among", "within", "across"], "'Between' is used for two."),
    ("She prefers tea ___ coffee.", "to", ["than", "over than", "from"], "'Prefer' takes 'to'."),
    ("The furniture ___ delivered yesterday.", "was", ["were", "are", "have been"], "'Furniture' is uncountable and singular."),
    ("He asked me where I ___.", "lived", ["live", "am living", "had live"], "Reported speech shifts the tense back."),
    ("Not only the students but also the teacher ___ confused.", "was", ["were", "are", "have"], "The verb agrees with the nearer subject 'teacher'."),
    ("I have never ___ such a beautiful painting.", "seen", ["saw", "see", "seeing"], "The present perfect needs the past participle."),
    ("The children are afraid ___ the dark.", "of", ["from", "with", "at"], "The phrase is 'afraid of'."),
    ("He will call you as soon as he ___ home.", "reaches", ["will reach", "reached", "is reaching"], "Time clauses use the simple present for future time."),
